# Branch and PR workflow

Full runbook: `.cursor/skills/how-to-branch-and-pr/SKILL.md`. Optional human log: `ticket_history.md`.

## Session gate (read first — non-negotiable)

**Each Cursor agent chat tab is one PR.** A new tab/thread is a **new session** even in the same repo, same branch checked out, or with a dirty tree left by another chat.

**Before the first `Write`/`StrReplace` in this tab** (including `.cursor/`, `docs/`, lint-only, or harness fixes):

1. `git branch --show-current` — if the branch name matches **another session's ticket/work**, do **not** keep editing on it.
2. `git status` — list pre-existing dirty paths; they are **foreign** to this PR unless the user explicitly folds them in here.
3. **This tab → this branch:** when git works: `git checkout main && git pull` (if remote exists), then `git checkout -b <project-prefix>-(<tag>)-<slug>`.

| Reject | Do instead |
|---|---|
| New chat, still on another tab’s feature branch, agent edits here | This tab creates **its own** branch before any edit |
| "Harness / lint only — skip branch" | Branch required for **every** tracked path, including `.cursor/` |
| Append this tab’s fix to another session’s open PR | One tab → one branch → one PR scope |
| Wait until "commit" or "open PR" to branch | Branch **before** the first edit in **this** tab |

If `.git` is incomplete (no objects / not a repo), **say so once**, skip branch commands, and edit in place — do not fake a git history.

Never append this tab’s edits onto another session’s branch unless the user **explicitly** combines PRs in this thread.

## Mandatory sequence (when git works)

1. Pull / update main before any new branch when a remote exists.
2. Feature branch before first repo edit: `<project-prefix>-(<tag>)-<kebab-slug>` (parentheses — git forbids `[` `]` in ref names). Title/commit: `<project-prefix>-[<tag>] - <words with spaces>`.
3. One Cursor chat tab = one agent session = one PR scope.
4. Scope gate before handback: `git status` / diffs must match **this session’s** edits only.
5. Agent rebases onto latest main before handback when possible; semantic conflicts → stop and ask.
6. **Handback is mandatory** — leave session edits **uncommitted**. Open with **WIP left uncommitted — you commit**. User commits, pushes, opens PR. Agent does **not** unless explicitly asked to commit.
7. **User merges** — agents never `gh pr merge`.

## Agent git permissions (hard boundary)

| Action | Agent |
|---|---|
| `git checkout`, `git checkout -b`, edit files | Yes — during implementation |
| `git fetch`, `git rebase`, stash/pop for rebase | Yes — before handback only |
| `git commit` | **Never** unless the user **explicitly** asks in this thread |
| `git push` / `gh pr create` / `gh pr merge` | **Never** |

**"Create/open the PR"** means: hand back suggested title, body, and exact commands for **you** to run.
